---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url.js';
---
<Base title="About" description="Engineer moving from civil and structural engineering in energy into product design and design strategy.">
  <div class="page about">
    <header>
      <p class="corner"><span class="figure-num">01</span> About</p>
      <h1 class="script about__title">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="about__grid">
      <div class="prose about__body">
        <p class="lede lede--small">
          I am an engineer, now studying design engineering at Harvard, after almost four
          years working across renewable energy and new-build nuclear.
        </p>

        <p>
          I studied Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering at UCL and joined Mott
          MacDonald straight afterwards, working first in Seoul and then in London. The
          first couple of years were in renewable energy, on offshore wind and solar.
          After that I moved onto new-build nuclear, mostly structural analysis and
          getting engineering, safety and environmental evidence into a form that
          stakeholders could make decisions from.
        </p>

        <p>
          The parts I was best at were the translations: turning a vague client
          requirement into something a team could build against, turning a technical
          constraint into a decision someone could take, and helping peer reviewers and
          regulators agree on what counted as sufficient evidence.
        </p>

        <p>
          I moved because of what the work was optimised for. Cost and programme are real
          constraints, but a solution can satisfy both and still land badly on the people
          who have to live with it. I started Harvard&rsquo;s Master in Design Engineering
          with preterm in early August 2026.
        </p>

        <h2>Two baselines</h2>

        <p>
          I grew up exposed to multiple cultures, which gives me a second reference point
          for what counts as a problem rather than just the way things are done. It shows
          up in how I work with people as much as in what I notice. I have worked in
          Korean and in English on the same projects, spent two years coordinating between
          teams in Seoul and London, and chaired a committee of twenty five representatives
          across Asia and Australasia serving a network of around three hundred members.
          Most of that job was making one group legible to another.
        </p>

        <h2>The engineering half</h2>

        <p>
          Almost everything I have worked on so far had to stand up. Offshore wind
          substructures, solar plants, then nuclear buildings, where a design is not
          finished when it looks right but when it has been checked against Eurocode and
          AISC and somebody independent agrees the numbers hold. I can build the model,
          run the analysis and verify it by hand.
        </p>

        <p>
          Few designers can take an idea that far, which is why I am useful earlier than
          the point where a concept usually gets handed over. I can say whether something
          can actually be built, what it would take to put up and take apart again, and
          which constraint is the one that will decide it.
        </p>

      </div>

      <aside class="about__side">
        {/* Temporarily removed at Elina's request. Put back by uncommenting.
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Looking for</p>
          <p>Summer 2027 internships in product design engineering, design technology, and hardware or systems design.</p>
        </div>
        */}
        <div class="about__card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
          <dl class="about__contact">
            <dt>Email, personal</dt>
            <dd><a href="mailto:elinahsyj@gmail.com">elinahsyj@gmail.com</a></dd>

            <dt>Email, Harvard</dt>
            <dd><a href="mailto:elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu">elina_lee@mde.harvard.edu</a></dd>

            <dt>LinkedIn</dt>
            <dd><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/ejl25" rel="me">linkedin.com/in/ejl25</a></dd>

            {/* GitHub, taken down for now at Elina's request.
            <dt>GitHub</dt>
            <dd><a href="https://github.com/shuiee" rel="me">github.com/shuiee</a></dd>
            */}
          </dl>
        </div>
        <p><a href={href('/cv/')}>Full CV &rarr;</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: var(--space-8); }
  .about__title {
    font-size: clamp(var(--size-8), 9vw, var(--size-10));
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-7);
  }
  .about__grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-8); }
  @media (min-width: 950px) {
    .about__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 260px; gap: var(--space-10); }
  }
  .about__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--size-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--border-hair) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .about__side { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); align-content: start; font-size: var(--size-2); }
  .about__card { border-top: var(--border-mark) solid var(--ink); padding-top: var(--space-3); }
  .about__card p + p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }

  /* Labelled so a reader can tell at a glance which address is which. */
  .about__contact { margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; }
  .about__contact dt {
    font-size: var(--size-1);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
  }
  .about__contact dd { margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; word-break: break-word; }
  .about__contact dd + dt { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
</style>
